+    // `snr` itself is never read again past RoundSnr() above, and `mode` is
+    // only ever used below via GetMcsForMode(mode)/its modulation class,
+    // both deterministic functions of the mode's own interned identity
+    // (GetUid()). So a cache hit on this exact key is guaranteed to return
+    // exactly what the uncached computation below would have produced: this
+    // is not an approximation, it is skipping recomputation of an
+    // already-fully-determined result. Only the table-lookup branch below
+    // is ever cached; GetMcsForMode() returning nullopt, or an out-of-range
